       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Per dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg. A 1600 mg dose is above that.\n- **Per day:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and lower is preferred. The risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise with dose, and a higher dose gives no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed for pain. This is the most common range.\n- 800 mg PO three times daily, which is 2,400 mg/day. This is often used for inflammatory conditions.\n- 800 mg PO four times daily, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the absolute ceiling and is only for selected cases.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg QID is intentional, tell me the indication. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy before it's entered."
      }
