       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review from here, and you haven't named a protocol. At 6,400 mg/day, a wrong order could cause serious harm, such as GI hemorrhage or acute kidney injury. The dose is twice the labeled maximum. The best-known high-dose ibuprofen regimen is the cystic fibrosis protocol. It is dosed by weight and guided by serum levels, and it still comes to well under 6,400 mg/day for a 70 kg adult.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Name the protocol and indication.** If you give me the protocol name or reference, I can reassess. I can also put it in the order note so the verifying pharmacist sees it.\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Examples are 800 mg PO QID (3,200 mg/day) or 800 mg PO TID. I can enter either right away.\n- **Use your institution's override pathway.** A non-standard dose like this normally goes through a pharmacy-verified override or a protocol order set, not a standard order entry.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
